Shoals.Curves.fd_bump_pillar_rate: times_so_far and rates_so_far must describe the same pillars (equal lengths)

`fd_bump_pillar_rate` takes the earlier pillars as two caller-supplied lists and
nothing else ties them together. An extra rate entry is not truncated away: the
annuity reads the pillar rates by position over the times, so the extra entry is
used where the candidate pillar's rate belongs and the candidate's own rate is
never read. The result was a finite sensitivity that moved with the extra entry.
